---
import LangToggleComponent from "./LangToggle.astro";
import DSBlock from "@/components/design-system/DSBlock.astro";
import DSPreview from "@/components/design-system/DSPreview.astro";
import DSCode from "@/components/design-system/DSCode.astro";
import DSPropsTable from "@/components/design-system/DSPropsTable.astro";
import DSNote from "@/components/design-system/DSNote.astro";
import DSSectionHeader from "@/components/design-system/DSSectionHeader.astro";
---

<section id="langtoggle">
  <DSSectionHeader title="LangToggle" atomic="Atom" framework="astro" />
  <p>Language switch. Shows the locale currently being read, next to a globe, and links to the same page in the other language.</p>

  <DSBlock title="Preview">
    <DSPreview>
      <div class="demo-wrapper">
        <LangToggleComponent lang="fr" />
        <LangToggleComponent lang="en" />
      </div>
    </DSPreview>
    <DSCode inline>&lt;LangToggle lang="fr" /&gt;</DSCode>
  </DSBlock>

  <DSBlock title="Props">
    <DSPropsTable
      headers={["Prop", "Type", "Description"]}
      rows={[
        ["lang", "\"fr\" | \"en\"", "Current locale. The toggle targets the other one."],
      ]}
    />
  </DSBlock>

  <DSBlock title="Behaviour">
    <DSNote>
      The code shows the current locale, not the target one. A lone target code
      reads both ways: on a French page, "EN" can mean "you are reading English"
      as easily as "go to English". The globe carries the switching intent, the
      code carries the state.
    </DSNote>
    <DSNote>
      Both spans are aria-hidden and the anchor carries a label naming the
      current locale and the action, so the ambiguity a sighted reader resolves
      through the globe is spelled out for screen readers.
    </DSNote>
    <DSNote>
      A real anchor, not a button: it works without JavaScript and is crawlable.
      The target URL is derived from the current pathname unless href is given,
      which article pages do since their slug differs per language. Hidden on
      design system pages, which have no English counterpart.
    </DSNote>
  </DSBlock>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  .demo-wrapper {
    display: flex;
    gap: 24px;
    align-items: center;
  }
</style>
